{"event_type":"review","id":"61b96eb9d2fcaf64694e567d320fb54e98165ddf10bf67346277a31ad9c6bf5c","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T23:56:44Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d6628ccda9bb54df138c968be62430e4ada97fd87ee7f1b2320581eebf9f5051","sha256":"d6628ccda9bb54df138c968be62430e4ada97fd87ee7f1b2320581eebf9f5051"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8a4ffb705f86972e31976f0214d1eb77cef5eec3c0ac6dcc915735d70723c357","sha256":"8a4ffb705f86972e31976f0214d1eb77cef5eec3c0ac6dcc915735d70723c357"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/772ef1a62dcc27cd8e35c4c92f4e994e0457c950e6423647a1bf6385e4ea83a9","sha256":"772ef1a62dcc27cd8e35c4c92f4e994e0457c950e6423647a1bf6385e4ea83a9"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a332096e854c3061a90a794373baba6898e5465aa8315f2672101de89acf1e4e","sha256":"a332096e854c3061a90a794373baba6898e5465aa8315f2672101de89acf1e4e"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b2a0aee8f4ec58c331b1762b08adb913aecb34e78d050685153af4975f5592e7","sha256":"b2a0aee8f4ec58c331b1762b08adb913aecb34e78d050685153af4975f5592e7"}],"attempt_id":"a4d86b60066220735eb01f1ea84e24cf429fb838e42bd55708b2bbd0b7d7cc9e:0:1","base":"bb87b046aa396439f4e8a528a6df0710fd050f78","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"1f975159915758997a6353a201bfe29ac7a96398","body":"**Treat failed ancestry probes as errors, not negative results.**\n\n`isAncestor` returns `call.code === 0`, so every nonzero status, including `128` and `null`, becomes `false`. Git uses status `1` for \"not an ancestor\" and other nonzero statuses for errors. In `reconcileCurrentRepair`, a `false` result skips the repair evidence without incrementing `deferred` or adding to `errors`. The run is still retried later, so the queue is not changed by the failed probe. The failure is still hidden from the result counts and diagnostics.\n\nReturn `true` only for status `0` and `false` only for status `1`. Throw for any other status. The existing `catch` in `reconcileCurrentRepair` then counts the failure as deferred and records the error.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-      return call.code === 0;\n+      if (call.code === 0) return true;\n+      if (call.code === 1) return false;\n+      throw new Error(`git merge-base --is-ancestor failed with status ${call.code}`);\n```\n\n</details>","id":"c44bf744a7700081fc86136a461123830687dec85b24ba8fe7ec1466a5f84f06","intervals":[[93,93]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/repairCurrentSource.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Treat failed ancestry probes as errors, not negative results."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"852a644f5a65ccd27036bdfc43f92b91b8e93590","body":"**Snapshot the batch dimensions when the call starts.**\n\nThe response check at `src/adapters/crq/reviewRegexMatcher.ts:68` reads `input.lines.length` when the worker's reply arrives. The worker receives a structured clone of the batch at submission, so it returns indexes for the submitted dimensions. The check compares those indexes against the caller's live array. If the caller clears or replaces `input.lines` before the promise settles, a valid hit such as `[0,0]` fails the bound. The call then rejects with `review matcher unavailable` even though the worker answered correctly.\n\n`readonly` in the parameter type is a compile-time annotation. It does not stop a caller from mutating the array it passed.\n\nRecord the rule and line counts when the call starts, then use those recorded values in every response bound and ordering check.","id":"104dfcd08b2b7d2b29e056f6337162c8937fa7a1a62d7758a0b48f3984f597cb","intervals":[[68,68]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/reviewRegexMatcher.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Snapshot the batch dimensions when the call starts."}],"head":"a8a9068e09110ff5e3ac3e78baa4793ce71104e6","head_tree":"bda143e5c3801b7c35ed31c000807c5f716cf6f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"d6d57016dfc7a577a1afa158eb1bd707ddee91c3","intervals":[[1,93]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/authorCapabilityMain.ts"},{"blob":"f9898f6034db7cef3bf59322420a2086adb4d593","intervals":[[1,110]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/authorEffects.ts"},{"blob":"f70b33b302ea4e7733928189a48f1335e22660ea","intervals":[[1,91]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewExit.ts"},{"blob":"830c0413326f46fd3379ac7da41ed3c5f7ac97b5","intervals":[[1,95]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/pushDiscoverySource.ts"},{"blob":"1f975159915758997a6353a201bfe29ac7a96398","intervals":[[1,96]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/repairCurrentSource.ts"},{"blob":"852a644f5a65ccd27036bdfc43f92b91b8e93590","intervals":[[1,81]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/reviewRegexMatcher.ts"},{"blob":"46812de99258d1e3fb1b42076cb4b7229d0deaca","intervals":[[1,99]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/rollingPrune.ts"},{"blob":"e83e1c0060a2b34067e46e3632b06dae36d3a2d4","intervals":[[1,99]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/slotSource.ts"}],"job_id":"a4d86b60066220735eb01f1ea84e24cf429fb838e42bd55708b2bbd0b7d7cc9e:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"d6d57016dfc7a577a1afa158eb1bd707ddee91c3","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/authorCapabilityMain.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"f9898f6034db7cef3bf59322420a2086adb4d593","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/authorEffects.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"f70b33b302ea4e7733928189a48f1335e22660ea","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewExit.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path clust